WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.140
In this video,

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.740
we try to understand one of the most interesting

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.580
three-dimensional shapes.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.500
It's called a prism.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.060
Most people think of a prism, as something like this.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.260
But have no idea about its correct definition.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.580
So let's erase this and start with the definition of a prism.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.620
It's a three-dimensional shape,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.400
a three-dimensional shape that has identical parallel ends

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.440
and all flat faces.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.260
Well, it's the most confusing definition ever!

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.260
Identical, parallel, flat there are just too many things.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.580
So forget the definition for now.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.400
Let's just look at figures and understand prisms.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.200
Look at this three-dimensional figure.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.980
The most important thing in topic of three-dimensional shapes,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.180
is visualizing the shapes.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.180
Few of the lines are dotted because those are the lines

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.640
that cannot be seen from this view.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.660
Look at the ends of this figure.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.200
It's a long figure with two ends.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.560
Now let me color the two ends for you.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.320
This figure has two triangles at its ends.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.160
And it has three rectangles as faces.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.480
This one in the front, one at the back and one at the bottom.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.080
Now we look at the definition.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.000
It says that the ends are identical and parallel.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.460
They are identical since both are triangles.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.600
And both the triangles are parallel to each other.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:34.980
The definition also says that all its faces should be flat.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:37.800
And in this figure, all faces are flat.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.140
They are rectangles.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.880
This by the way, is called a triangular prism.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.440
Here's another three-dimensional shape.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.500
Let me color its ends.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.960
We can see that it has two rectangles as ends.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.520
And they are also parallel to each other.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.020
And it has four rectangles as faces.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.660
One on the right hand side,

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.420
one on the left hand side,

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.060
one at the top and one at the bottom.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.880
So all its faces are flat.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.440
This is called a rectangular prism.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.440
So if you noticed the prisms are defined by its ends.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.840
Triangles as its ends, triangular prism.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.700
Rectangles at its ends, rectangular prism.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.160
Look at the rectangular prism.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.460
Does this shape remind you of another three-dimensional shape?

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.920
Yes, a rectangular prism is also a cuboid.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.600
Now let's look at a few figures and understand if they are prisms are not.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.540
Remember the definition,

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:44.180
identical parallel ends and all flat surfaces.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.640
Here's the first figure.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.400
It's a part of a pipe.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.280
Both the ends are circles

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.400
and are parallel to each other.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.900
It means that this figure has identical parallel ends.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.120
This figure has identical parallel ends,

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.900
but has a curved surface.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.160
Hence, it's not a prism.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.920
I want to emphasize,

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.920
there are only two things that make a three-dimensional shape

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.200
a prism.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.960
Identical and parallel ends and all its faces flat.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.480
Here, the ends are flat but the surface is curved.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.840
So it's not a prism.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.740
Here's another figure.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.940
First, we look at the ends.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.720
Both are triangles,

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.520
and hence we can say that this figure has identical ends.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.060
But wait,

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.660
they are not parallel.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.240
The upper triangle is slightly tilted.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.200
So this figure as well,

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.980
is not a prism.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.100
Now assume we have a plane with a rectangle on it.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.600
If we project the rectangle upwards,

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.280
equally from all sides,

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.720
we get a prism.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.420
In this figure, we have projected all the sides to the same height.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:59.180
But what if we do not project all the sides to equal heights?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.920
If we do not project it equally, like in this figure,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.580
we do not get a prism.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:10.180
This is not a prism as its ends are not parallel.

